Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think maybe by now the book, I'm not sure if it's empty, but Wolfram is going to tell us,\N而且我认为现在这本书，我不确定是不是空的，但沃尔弗拉姆会告诉我们。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.64,0:00:06.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think, his thoughts about what are the remaining challenges if we want to realize embodied AI.\N我认为，他思考的是，如果我们想实现具身AI，还面临哪些未解决的挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.24,0:00:09.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So let's give a warm welcome to Wolfram.\N让我们热烈欢迎沃尔弗拉姆。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.48,0:00:13.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks, Dieter.\N谢谢，迪特。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.64,0:00:14.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's take a selfie.\N来拍张自拍吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.31,0:00:19.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks.\N谢谢。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.75,0:00:22.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And thanks for having me here.\N谢谢你们邀请我来这里。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.33,0:00:25.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,I must confess, I'm super nervous right now.\N我得承认，我现在超级紧张。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.83,0:00:30.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's actually my very first plenary speech in robotics,\N这实际上是我在机器人领域发表的首次全体会议演讲。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.43,0:00:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,at least in the robotics and automation society space, and never stood in front of such a big audience.\N至少在机器人与自动化协会的领域里，从未站在如此庞大的观众面前。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.75,0:00:40.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so it's really great to be here.\N所以能在这里真的非常高兴。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.81,0:00:47.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,This talk is a little bit about my perspective or my vision on where\N这次演讲，我想分享一下我对未来的看法或愿景。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.49,0:00:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,we might be going in this right now race about embodied AI systems or robots.\N我们可能正处在人形机器人或具身AI系统竞赛的途中。
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.91,0:01:01.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it also will, I will take you back a little bit, maybe like 30 years ago.\N而且我还要带你们回到过去，大概30年前的样子。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.53,0:01:07.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,But at some point in time, we'll even take you even further back, something like two to 3000 years ago.\N但总有一天，我们会带你回到更久远的过去，比如两千到三千年前。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.49,0:01:09.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,I will let you know at that particular time.\N到时候我会告诉你的。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.49,0:01:14.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we will then see what is behind all of this.\N然后我们就能看到这一切背后的真相。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.48,0:01:20.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this talk would not be possible with all my friends and colleagues, normally talks end with this.\N所以这次演讲能顺利完成，离不开我所有朋友和同事的支持，通常演讲都会以这个结尾。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.12,0:01:22.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to start with this.\N我先从这个开始。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.70,0:01:28.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,I have so many friends who contributed to that that I cannot actually add pictures, would have taken me years.\N我有很多朋友都为此做出了贡献，我实在没法一一配上图片，那得花上好几年时间。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.18,0:01:37.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thank all my friends and colleagues who contributed to that work, and a few will be listed and even be shown in pictures here in this presentation.\N我要感谢所有为此项工作做出贡献的朋友和同事，其中几位将在本次演示中被列出，甚至还会在图片中出现。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.33,0:01:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So my view in robotics is actually that that we are going to be or to\N所以我在机器人领域的看法是，我们将会或正在
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.16,0:01:51.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,have a that we are having actually super useful tool for helping us solving important societal problems.\N我们实际上拥有一个非常有用的工具，能帮助我们解决重要的社会问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.54,0:01:57.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be traffic and it can be particularly seen here where you can actually see\N让它成为交通，这里尤其明显，你可以清楚看到
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.38,0:02:05.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,multiple companies with driverless cars driving around making our traffic more effective and also hopefully safer.\N多家公司正在运营无人驾驶汽车，让交通更加高效，也希望能更安全。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.62,0:02:11.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,It can be the case in production where we are in a global race about the most efficient\N在实际生产中，我们正面临一场全球范围内的效率竞赛。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.30,0:02:20.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,production systems and so on and where we are believing that robotics will help us competing in that space.\N生产系统等，我们认为机器人将帮助我们在这一领域保持竞争力。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.01,0:02:25.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there is assistance and healthcare, the next dimension, we will talk about this as well,\N然后是医疗和健康辅助，这是下一个维度，我们也会谈到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.81,0:02:32.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,this question of how can we actually build robots that help us with elderly care and also support us in our homes.\N如何真正打造能帮助老年人护理并支持我们居家生活的机器人。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.39,0:02:39.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,And finally we are living on a finite sphere and actually constantly growing the fastest growth is\N最后，我们生活在一个有限的球体上，而实际上，我们正不断增长，增长最快的时候正是现在。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.81,0:02:46.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,in this space here this room it's probably this fastest growing society on earth and that's also something\N这个空间，这个房间，可能是地球上发展最快的社群，这一点同样值得关注。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.63,0:02:53.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need to support or hoped to be able to support with robotics and in fact for\N我们需要通过机器人来支持，事实上也希望能借助机器人实现支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.20,0:02:59.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we need that what is called intelligent robots robots that perceive their world like maybe reason about\N我们需要的是所谓的智能机器人，能够像人类一样感知世界并进行推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.12,0:03:04.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,it create models about it and then execute actions in order to achieve their goals That's basically\N它会创建关于自身的模型，然后执行行动以实现目标。这基本上就是
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.76,0:03:10.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,that what we are interested in and right now we are working on that what is called embodied\N这正是我们关注的，目前我们正在研究所谓的具身化。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.08,0:03:17.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,robotics and or embodied AI as a potential solution to this and I love these Pictures with humanoids\N机器人学或具身AI可能是解决这一问题的潜在方案，我非常喜欢这些具身机器人的图片。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.90,0:03:25.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,all these, by the way, disclaimer: all pictures that contain white humanoids are generated with generative AI, right?\N顺便说一下，免责声明：所有包含白色人形机器人的图片都是用生成式AI生成的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.52,0:03:29.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,all the others are basically handmade and And here are a couple of solutions where we\N其他所有产品基本上都是手工制作的，而这里有几个解决方案，我们
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.82,0:03:35.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,envision this to be done in mostly like right now using that what is called humanoid robots.\N设想现在就用这类人形机器人来完成这项任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.70,0:03:40.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,The reason why humanoids are envisioned to be one of the solutions here is that\N之所以认为人形机器人是这里的一个解决方案，是因为
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.34,0:03:47.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,they will allow us to make a smooth transition from actually manual production towards automated production.\N它们将帮助我们顺利实现从人工生产向自动化生产的过渡。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.98,0:03:50.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we can even have this what is called mixed production,\N因此我们甚至可以实现所谓的混合生产，
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.82,0:03:59.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we have human and robot co-workers in the same space on the same tasks with the same tools, basically accomplishing the very same tasks.\N我们让人类和机器人在同一空间内，使用相同的工具，共同完成几乎完全相同的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.18,0:04:02.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is why humanoids are so much hyped these days.\N这就是为什么人形机器人如今如此受追捧。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.46,0:04:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But on top of this, there's also the next hype.\N但除此之外，还有下一个热潮。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.72,0:04:13.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was in China twice this year and saw like several hundred startups in the space of humanoid robots.\N今年我两次到中国，短短时间内就看到了几百家专注于人形机器人领域的初创公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.54,0:04:17.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And on top of this, equally many startups in the space of robotic hands.\N此外，还有数量相当的初创企业专注于机器人手领域。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.06,0:04:24.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the reason for this is that in order to perform dexterous manipulations with tools that we also use we need to have proper hands But it's not\N之所以如此，是因为要像我们一样使用工具进行灵巧操作，就必须拥有合适的手。但事实并非如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.32,0:04:29.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,only about mechanics It's also about perception and now we'll come to this in\N仅仅关于机械还远远不够，它还关乎感知，接下来我们将深入探讨这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.28,0:04:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,this talk as well And finally and this was mentioned by Peter stone earlier today.\N本次演讲也涉及这一点，最后，这正如彼得·斯通今天早些时候提到的。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.00,0:04:45.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,You also need Computing on a large scale and on a larger scale than it was available thus far for at least university-like research.\N你还需要大规模的计算能力，而且规模要大于迄今为止所能提供的，至少要达到大学级研究的需求。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.06,0:04:53.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,But on top of this, and this is something that is mostly underestimated by investors and so on and so forth and even politicians,\N但除此之外，这一点往往被投资者、政界人士等低估了。
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.94,0:05:02.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,is this problem of building an AI system that can actually control these robots to accomplish these tasks.\N这个问题在于，如何构建一个AI系统，使其真正能够控制这些机器人完成各项任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.72,0:05:08.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have made an enormous progress over the past years when it comes to building the hardware for this,\N在构建这一硬件方面，我们过去几年取得了巨大进展。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.58,0:05:17.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,also enhance humanoids for me it's has been just crazy but building the AI is still the challenge that we are\N还让我感到惊讶的是，人形机器人也变得非常疯狂，但构建AI仍然是我们面临的挑战。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.14,0:05:24.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,facing right and now ask like robot learning is it right and that's actually what I believe right the only way\N朝右面对着，现在像机器人学习一样问：对吗？这恰恰就是我的信念，唯一的途径
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.72,0:05:33.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,for solving this is right robot learning and if you boil this even further down then this is this community over\N解决这个问题的关键在于机器人学习，而进一步简化来看，这正是这个社区的核心所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.56,0:05:40.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,here it's basically the core community that is working on this topic and where I believe this is going to take us,\N这里基本上是专注于这一议题的核心社群，我认为它将引领我们走向未来。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.66,0:05:43.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,hopefully, there where we want to go.\N希望我们能到达那个地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.39,0:05:49.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is our journey more than 2,000 years back.\N这就是我们追溯两千多年的历史旅程。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.37,0:05:55.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is, according to Greek mythology, this is the King Sisyphus.\N根据希腊神话，这就是国王西西弗斯。
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.41,0:06:07.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And he was, because he believed that he was more intelligent than Zeus, the most important god in Greek mythology, and Zeus didn't really like that.\N因为他相信自己比希腊神话中最重要的神宙斯还要聪明，而宙斯并不太喜欢这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.39,0:06:13.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,Turns out that kind of like reflects also sometimes our thinking here, right?\N原来这种想法也反映了我们有时的思维方式，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.50,0:06:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Everyone of us believes to be the most intelligent person in the world, right?\N我们每个人都觉得自己是世界上最聪明的人，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.48,0:06:19.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's something that researchers mostly need to do.\N这主要是研究人员需要完成的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.24,0:06:26.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,And Zeus got so upset about this that he condemned Sisyphus to actually take a large boulder up a hill.\N宙斯对此极为愤怒，于是下令让西西弗斯将一块巨大的石头推上山顶。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.98,0:06:32.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this thing here is the boulder that this poor guy was condemned to transport up the hill.\N所以这个东西就是那个可怜人被判处要推上山的巨石。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.40,0:06:35.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not that this was enough of a for this guy,\N但这对这家伙来说还不够。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.66,0:06:43.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,Zeus actually condemned this Boulder so that it always fell down when Sisyphus was close to the summit of this mountain And\N宙斯实际上诅咒了这块石头，使得当西西弗斯快要到达山顶时，石头总是会滚落下去。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.94,0:06:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,then the boulder actually rolled down the entire hill and this guy had to start from scratch You might not ask this question.\N然后巨石真的滚下了整座山，这家伙不得不从头开始。你可能不会问这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.64,0:06:52.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,What does this have to do with our research?\N这跟我们的研究有什么关系？
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.90,0:07:00.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's basically that like when you look at that what we are doing is we are basically Finding some sort of technology.\N本质上，当我们看那个时，我们所做的就是寻找某种技术。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.57,0:07:02.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be Probabilistic Robotics.\N就叫它概率机器人学吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.63,0:07:05.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let it be deep learning Let it be foundation models, right?\N让它成为深度学习，让它成为基础模型，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.01,0:07:10.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,We are believing that this technology is finally going to help us getting this boulder\N我们相信，这项技术终于能帮我们搬走这块巨石。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.97,0:07:16.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,up the hill and Unfortunately so far right you were not really successful with this,\Nuphill, and unfortunately so far,\Nyou haven't really succeeded with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.65,0:07:17.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.15,0:07:25.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,So somehow like some God actually through this boulder again down and this road down and yet to start from scratch again This is why what\N所以不知怎的，仿佛有位神明又把这块巨石推了下来，这条路又得从头开始。这正是为何……
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.31,0:07:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,this has from my perspective to do or this see like kind of the metaphor that is matching that what has actually happened in in our\N从我的角度来看，这似乎正是与我们实际经历的情况相匹配的隐喻。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.31,0:07:37.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,community and when you look at technologies I've been involved in the detail\N社区，当你审视我曾参与过的技术细节时
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.89,0:07:41.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,already mentioned I mean there have been three important boulders that I worked\N我之前已经提到过，我参与过的三个重要项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.79,0:07:47.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,on and it started in 1995 who actually was born at that time\N而且它始于1995年，当时实际上有人出生了
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.33,0:07:55.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,already 1995 five percent or so of this audience here right which is which\N早在1995年，这里在座的观众中就有大约5%的人了。
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.76,0:08:00.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,is pretty cool this when we actually started working on this with the\N这真的很酷，当我们真正开始着手这项工作时
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.12,0:08:06.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,belief that we could actually solve everything by probabilistic reasoning right and like\N相信我们实际上可以通过概率推理解决所有问题，就是这样
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.20,0:08:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,this was basically the time when we created this book, Probabilistic Robotics; there is Sebastian, Dieter and me right in\N这基本上是我们创作《概率机器人学》这本书的时期，旁边是塞巴斯蒂安、迪特尔和我。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.48,0:08:28.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,car at that point in time which basically came out of this of the success of the Probabilistic Robotics theory or like concept in the context\N那个时刻的汽车，基本上源于概率机器人学理论或概念的成功。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.12,0:08:34.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,of Autonomous driving right and to here in the bottom you even see the three of us on the summit of the mount of a mountain Unfortunately,\N自动驾驶的右边，下方你甚至能看到我们三个人站在山顶上。可惜的是，
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.54,0:08:38.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,it's not the same mountains to the first force condemned to carry the boulder up.\N那不是同一座山，对第一个被迫背负巨石攀登的人来说。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.74,0:08:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was from Mount Rainier instead so so this is basically the equations that are underlying there and that led to an enormous success in the space\N它来自雷尼尔山，因此这基本上是支撑其背后的方程，也正是这些方程带来了太空领域的巨大成功。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.24,0:08:53.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,of Autonomous driving and it's basically that what you see outside these self\N自动驾驶，基本上就是你看到的这些车外面的自主驾驶
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.06,0:08:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,-driving cars are basically governed by this equation over here which is state estimation.\N自动驾驶汽车基本上由这处的方程所控制，也就是状态估计。
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.24,0:09:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,And we are basically trying to figure out where the vehicle is given a map of the environment.\N我们基本上是在尝试根据环境地图确定车辆的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.56,0:09:10.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And when it comes to building self-driving cars, you need to solve basically three tasks.\N说到打造自动驾驶汽车，你基本上需要解决三个任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.78,0:09:13.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first one is stay on the road, which is localization.\N第一个是保持在道路上，也就是定位。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.66,0:09:15.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,The second one is don't get hit.\N第二个是别被击中。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.54,0:09:17.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the third one is don't hit anything.\N第三，别碰到任何东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.30,0:09:21.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And once you are able to do all this, you're getting really, really far.\N一旦你能够做到这一切，你就真正走得很远了。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.90,0:09:29.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's this entire thing in action in indoors and outdoors and GPS denied environments and then you ask\N而且这是整个系统在室内、室外以及无GPS环境下的实际运行效果，然后你提问
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.06,0:09:34.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,the question like how accurate is this actually we also did some experiments a few years ago just to give\N这个问题，比如这个准确度到底有多高，我们几年前也做过一些实验，就是为了给个参考
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.28,0:09:42.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,you an intuition how accurately you can actually localize a robot on a factory floor then these black stripes here\N你大概能直观地感受到，你实际上能在工厂地板上多准确地定位一个机器人，然后看这里的黑条纹
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.04,0:09:48.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,that are not used for localization they are actually indicating how accurate this platform is when you want to see\N那些未用于定位的，实际上反映了该平台在你想要查看时的准确性。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.70,0:09:55.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,this in more quantities then you can see down here in these statistics that the accuracy in localization in post\N这里的定位准确率，比你在此处统计数据中看到的要高得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:09:55.62,0:10:05.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,estimation is around a millimeter and who believes that this can be achieved with foundation models as well nobody okay\N估计误差约为一毫米，还有人相信基础模型也能实现这一点，好吧
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.01,0:10:13.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I maybe in a few years from now detail as well which is good so but this is kind of\N也许几年后我也会详细说明，这很好，但情况大致如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.11,0:10:23.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,like the the outcome of this endeavor Probabilistic Robotics and that led to these self driving cars and you can\N就像这一努力的成果——概率机器人学，它催生了自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:23.45,0:10:31.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,see a typical software stack of self-driving cars and those components where I think Probabilistic Robotics is particularly\N看看自动驾驶汽车的典型软件栈，以及我认为概率机器人学特别重要的那些组件
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.27,0:10:40.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,strong and it's in fact this mapping and localization task here is an application to to mapping it's basically the\N强大，事实上，这里的地图构建与定位任务正是地图应用的体现，本质上就是地图构建。
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.07,0:10:47.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,equations underlying slam and this is a company that I found a ten years ago that is like concerned with\NSLAM 的基本方程，这是一家我十年前创立的公司，专注于相关领域
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.59,0:10:54.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,3d mapping of real estate buildings and also historic buildings also several hundred years ago like the Leaning Tower of\N房地产建筑以及历史建筑的三维地图，甚至包括数百年前的建筑，比如比萨斜塔
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.89,0:11:01.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Pisa we created with this technology the most accurate model of this of this tower it's an indoor outdoor model\N我们用这项技术打造了这座塔最精确的模型，它是一个室内外一体化的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.79,0:11:10.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,basically which is super useful for cultural heritage preservation so on top of this we also created the most accurate\N这在文化遗产保护方面非常有用，此外我们还打造了迄今为止最精准的模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.73,0:11:21.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,model of the Freiburg Cathedral that was depicted on this page over here why this actually was a major stepping\N弗莱堡大教堂的模型，就在这页上所描绘的那样，这实际上是一个重要的跨越
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.07,0:11:30.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,stone towards building self-driving cars and created super useful tools for these vehicles and when it comes to perception,\N致力于打造自动驾驶汽车，并为这些车辆开发了极为实用的工具，而在感知方面，
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.67,0:11:36.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,tracking, localization, prediction, planning and control, it also introduced the problem.\N跟踪、定位、预测、规划和控制，同时也提出了这一问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.21,0:11:48.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,The fact that we were relying on these high definition maps actually made these vehicles being bound towards, we call this level 4 automation,\N我们依赖高清地图的事实，实际上让这些车辆被限定在所谓的四级自动化范围内。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.73,0:11:55.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is basically automation in geofenced areas, which is exactly what you're seeing right now with self-driving cars.\N这本质上就是地理围栏区域内的自动化，正是你现在看到的自动驾驶汽车所实现的。
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.41,0:12:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,You see them in several cities, but you don't see them overall in the world, which would be level 5.\N你在几个城市能看到它们，但你不会在全球范围内看到它们，那才是第五级。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.21,0:12:07.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,Where do you think are we with robotics right now when it comes to manipulation?\N在操作能力方面，你认为我们目前的机器人技术处于什么水平？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.45,0:12:08.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is who's for level 3?\N这是谁要达到三级水平？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.92,0:12:12.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe a few level 4?\N也许有几个四级？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.16,0:12:14.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Level 5?\NLevel 5？
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.04,0:12:16.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,One.\N一。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.18,0:12:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are in fact a few applications for this, but I think the major problem there is implementing this everywhere in the world.\N事实上，这类应用确实存在一些，但我认为主要问题在于如何在全球范围内实现普及。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.35,0:12:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this has been the major challenge, it's also like a driving force for me nowadays, this question of can we actually get rid of these maps.\N这一直是我当前面临的主要挑战，同时也是推动我的核心动力——我们是否真的能摆脱这些地图。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.59,0:12:45.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,These maps have been super useful and we roboticists like 3D maps simply because it is geometry and we know very well how to deal with geometry.\N这些地图非常有用，我们机器人工程师特别喜欢3D地图，因为它们是几何结构，\N而我们非常熟悉如何处理几何问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.91,0:12:52.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,roboticists love geometry and by building these maps we turn navigation problems in geometry problems\N机器人学家热爱几何学，通过构建这些地图，我们将导航问题转化为几何问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.87,0:12:59.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,and there we go there we are with all the constraints regarding the complexity of environments.\N好了，我们完成了，所有关于环境复杂性的约束都已考虑在内。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.34,0:13:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next step in that direction then was like here again is Probabilistic Robotics was\N那么朝着这个方向的下一步就是，再次出现概率机器人学
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.66,0:13:09.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,the deep network hype right so when you look back at at the give me\N深度网络的炒作热潮，所以当你回过头来看
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.02,0:13:15.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,a second Probabilistic Robotics then you basically see that we are particularly bad at this\N第二个概率机器人学，你就会发现我们在这一点上表现特别差
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.12,0:13:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,first step making semantics out of the sensor data like understanding images and understanding point clouds.\N第一步是从传感器数据中提取语义，例如理解图像和点云。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.04,0:13:31.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is something that deep networks actually substantially improved and it was a second revolution in this space.\N这是深度网络真正带来显著提升的领域，也是该领域的第二次革命。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.66,0:13:38.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's one example for this deep learning application which is semantic segmentation and there\N这里有一个深度学习应用的例子，即语义分割。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.58,0:13:44.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can basically see that like these systems are substantially better in this interpretation part.\N你可以明显看出，这些系统在理解部分的表现要好得多。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.56,0:13:49.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you agreed with me that they are not as good in localization and mapping.\N而且你同意我的看法，它们在定位和地图构建方面并不那么出色。
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.02,0:13:55.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then obviously that raises a question like is there a way to combine the two, right?\N然后显然会引出一个问题：有没有办法把两者结合起来呢？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.20,0:13:56.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,How can we do this properly?\N我们该如何正确地做到这一点？
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.72,0:14:06.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is something, a discussion that I also started with colleagues here and we were at a TRI or we worked at TRI building these self-driving cars,\N这是个话题，我也和这里的同事讨论过。当时我们在 TRI，\N或者我们在 TRI 工作，正在打造这些自动驾驶汽车。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.28,0:14:11.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,namely this question of once we have these super effective segmentation and\N也就是说，一旦我们有了这种极为高效的分割能力，
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.56,0:14:16.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,Perception tools like how can we combine them properly with this probabilistic approach?\N感知工具，比如我们该如何将它们与这种概率方法恰当地结合？
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.16,0:14:23.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you need there in this context is basically that what is called Calibrated uncertainties and otherwise your filters\N但在这个语境下，你真正需要的是所谓的校准不确定性，否则你的滤波器就会失效。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.94,0:14:29.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,or your state estimation processes will basically diverge This problem doesn't go away when you go to foundation models\N否则你的状态估计过程将基本发散。这个问题在转向基础模型后依然存在。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.74,0:14:37.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,It becomes even harder because these models are even more complex and like estimating or proper Uncertainties based on\N这变得更加困难，因为这些模型更加复杂，且基于不确定性进行准确估计也更加困难。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.94,0:14:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,these foundation models is a severe change And here's one example of that what we did in this context,\N这些基座模型带来了重大变革，以下是在这一背景下我们所做的一项示例。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.96,0:14:50.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,this uncertainty where panoptic segmentation where you basically not only provide\N这种不确定性体现在全景分割中，你不仅需要提供分割结果
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.03,0:14:56.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,the segmentation masks but you also get these semantic uncertainties for segmentation.\N分割掩码的同时，你还能获得分割的语义不确定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.71,0:15:00.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can also do this for instant segmentation which then turns out to be\N你也可以对实时分割执行此操作，结果发现
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.33,0:15:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you combine the two to be just panoptic segmentation or some panoptic uncertainties.\N如果你将两者结合，就变成了全景分割或某种全景不确定性。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.61,0:15:12.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here you see this in action for like famous data set you can actually see that these\N在这里，你可以看到它在著名数据集上的实际应用，你甚至能清楚地看到这些
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.51,0:15:21.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,uncertainties arise at places where they actually make sense that's namely at the borders of classes or also objects\N不确定性出现在它们实际上有意义的地方，也就是类别或物体的边界处。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.04,0:15:31.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,right the and the next step was basically the integration of that with one of these state estimation processes\N然后下一步基本上就是将其与其中一种状态估计算法进行集成。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.34,0:15:37.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,you see in this context a particle filter in which case you would actually you actually need to estimate\N在这种情况下，你看到的是一个粒子滤波器，这时你实际上需要进行估计
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.08,0:15:44.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,a regularizer that takes the uncertainties that are generated by the networks in order to convert them into\N一种正则化方法，利用网络生成的不确定性将其转化为
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.70,0:15:49.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,calibrated uncertainties which is something that you actually need to learn and when you do this in a proper\N校准后的不确定性，这是你需要真正去学习的东西，当你以正确的方式进行时
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.44,0:15:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,fashion then you can actually have probabilistic localization at a higher accuracy based on these deep network outputs or\N时尚领域，你实际上可以根据这些深度网络的输出，实现更高精度的概率定位。
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.16,0:16:08.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,learned outputs from directly from the data into segmentation mask and other features that you are actually interested in.\N直接从数据中学习输出，生成你真正感兴趣的分割掩码及其他特征。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.72,0:16:20.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which brings me to this this other problem in this context right so what we did in this deep learning phase was basically we were in the\N这让我想到在这种背景下另一个问题。在深度学习阶段，我们实际上处于
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.29,0:16:26.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,belief that we can actually solve all these problems using deep learning with\N相信我们实际上可以通过深度学习解决所有这些问题
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.12,0:16:33.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,the complicating factor that we actually had to collect a ton of data like\N我们实际上不得不收集大量数据，这是其中的一个复杂因素。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.08,0:16:40.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,in a supervised fashion maybe We also believe that we can do this in a semi-supervised way on the fly while the vehicle is actually operating\N以监督方式或许可行，我们还相信，可以在车辆实际运行时，实时地以半监督的方式实现这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.36,0:16:43.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,But what we mostly needed to specify is that what is called an\N但我们需要明确的是，所谓的
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.96,0:16:50.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,ontology we needed to provide the vehicle with background information What are the right?\N我们需要为车辆提供背景信息，即什么是正确的？
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.60,0:16:57.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,classes that are of interest in this particular task for The vehicle namely self-driving\N在此特定任务中，车辆自动驾驶所关注的类别
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.39,0:17:04.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,but now assume you do have like a robot that is supposed to Like tidy up\N但现在假设你确实有一个机器人，它应该负责整理收拾
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.71,0:17:10.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,a kitchen right this problem of like here There's a kitchen and the robot should clean\N一个厨房，这里的问题是，有一个厨房，机器人应该去清理。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.89,0:17:17.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,it up And this question of like do we need maps in which classes are relevant?\N这问题在于，我们是否需要地图来确定哪些类别是相关的？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.15,0:17:22.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Depends highly on the question of what actually does this kitchen look like and\N这很大程度上取决于这个厨房实际上长什么样。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.75,0:17:27.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,now imagine This is a kitchen like that the robot encounters after a student party,\N现在想象一下，这是一间学生派对过后，机器人遇到的厨房。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.85,0:17:30.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,right which might look like this over here, right?\N对，可能看起来就像这里这样，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.50,0:17:32.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And obviously like I mean,\N显然，我的意思是，
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.32,0:17:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can zoom in here to actually make this a little bit more visible Like creating a three\N我可以在这里放大，让这个看起来更清晰一点，比如创建一个三维效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.76,0:17:46.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,-dimensional model of this environment with is extremely hard Potentially also not super useful and also defining all the\N对这个环境的三维模型进行构建极其困难，可能也并非特别有用，而且定义所有细节也十分繁琐。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.62,0:17:53.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,classes that you need in order to solve this Clean up the kitchen tasks are extremely hard to\N你需要的课程才能解决这个清理厨房的任务非常难以掌握。
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.86,0:18:01.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,define a priori And this is where from my perspective this limit of this deep learning phase has been.\N预先定义。从我的角度来看，这就是深度学习阶段的局限所在。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.98,0:18:08.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was super useful in the context of self-driving because self-driving is a much more controlled environment.\N在自动驾驶的背景下非常有用，因为自动驾驶是一个更加受控的环境。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.94,0:18:15.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's kind of, from my perspective, this very same as having robots on factory floors versus having robots at home.\N从我的角度来看，这和工厂里的机器人与家里的机器人没什么区别。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.37,0:18:26.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why I believe that we will much faster be on factory floors with these platforms rather than in real messy homes as we see here.\N这就是为什么我认为，我们将会更快地在工厂车间部署这些平台，\N而不是像这里看到的那样在真实杂乱的家中应用。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.85,0:18:31.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And unfortunately, the real world is typically very messy.\N遗憾的是，现实世界通常非常混乱。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.68,0:18:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which brings us to the last point, which is foundation models, which really,\N这就引出了最后一个观点，即基础模型，这实际上
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.00,0:18:40.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,when I interacted with them for the very first time, they really blew my mind.\N第一次和他们互动时，他们真的让我大开眼界。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.02,0:18:45.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I thought, oh my goodness, this is the next stepping stone in robotics.\N我想，天哪，这将是机器人技术的下一个飞跃。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.40,0:18:47.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I truly believe that is the case.\N我真心相信情况确实如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.78,0:18:51.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's the third time we are carrying up the boulder of the hill.\N所以我们第三次把石头推上山了。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.72,0:18:56.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is basically what I believe is happening right now.\N所以这基本上就是我认为现在正在发生的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.18,0:19:04.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's a few examples of a few works that we worked on in the past This is the so-called vision language maps.\N这里有几个我们过去完成的作品示例，这是所谓的视觉语言地图。
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.12,0:19:10.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have you basically at the very beginning of this hype Used like the embeddings that we\N我们基本上正处于这场热潮的起点，就像我们使用的嵌入向量一样
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.60,0:19:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,at that time Still mapped to a 3d voxel grid in order to actually perform semantic navigation tasks\N当时仍映射到三维体素网格，以执行语义导航任务
