Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.06,0:29:33.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,them So the idea there basically was like taking elementary skills that are still sufficiently complicated like opening a\N所以那个想法本质上是，选取一些仍然足够复杂的初级技能，比如开门。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:33.94,0:29:41.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,drawer and Then chaining them using an LLM You saw this earlier today as well using the LLM\N抽屉，然后使用大语言模型将它们串联起来。你今天早些时候也见过这种用法。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:41.18,0:29:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,as a programming assistant that changed these elementary actions based on the input that you get from the images\N作为编程助手，它会根据你从图像中获取的输入，动态调整这些基础操作
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.84,0:29:55.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,in order to Get a concrete program for the robot to execute this particular task Right and these elementary\N为了使机器人执行这一特定任务，必须提供一个具体的程序。
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.96,0:30:04.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,skills that they were trained using so-called play data with like assigned language labels in the very end\N他们所掌握的技能，是通过所谓的游戏数据训练得来的，最后才被赋予了语言标签。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.42,0:30:11.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then based on the context of the scene we could basically have the robot executing this more\N然后根据场景的上下文，我们可以让机器人基本执行这个操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.00,0:30:19.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,complex tasks then in the end this can be as abstract as heat please tidy up the workspace and\N复杂任务，最后甚至可以抽象到“请整理工作区”这样的指令。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.93,0:30:25.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,then depending on what is in display in the space in the context and the actions to be generated\N然后根据上下文中的显示内容和需要生成的动作而定
Dialogue: 0,0:30:25.27,0:30:32.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,like to get a sequence of actions to execute this particular task and then here's this entire system in\N想要获得一连串动作来执行这个特定任务，然后这里就是整个系统
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.31,0:30:37.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,action like we basically see the robot like open it inferring that it needs to open the drawer\N动作就像我们看到机器人在推断需要打开抽屉，于是打开了它
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.19,0:30:43.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,first then puts the blocks into the drawer closes the drawer and then attempts to actually push the green\N然后把积木放进抽屉，关上抽屉，再尝试真正推动绿色的物体。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.63,0:30:53.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,button I think things like this are super important I mean there's obviously an important debate about is this\N按钮，我认为这类事情非常重要，毕竟关于这是否重要，显然存在一场重要的讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.82,0:31:00.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,the right way for doing this like turning this into these programs or using these LLMs as programming assistants,\N正确的方法是将这些程序化，或把大型语言模型用作编程助手。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:00.40,0:31:05.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,or can we do this end-to-end directly using a VLA, right?\N或者我们能否直接使用视觉-语言-动作模型端到端完成，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:05.92,0:31:11.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,But this is something that we as a society might hopefully figure out in the near future.\N但这是我们社会有望在不久的将来共同解决的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:13.18,0:31:19.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's other aspects as well that I find super interesting in this context of manipulation.\N在操作这个语境下，还有其他一些方面让我觉得非常有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.18,0:31:26.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we see plenty of manipulation papers here, which are absolutely impressive.\N我的意思是，这里有很多操纵相关的论文，都非常令人印象深刻。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.65,0:31:34.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,that the question that I wondered about when I thought about this was this question of how do we actually interact with objects\N当我思考这个问题时，我一直在想，我们究竟该如何与物体进行交互。
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.81,0:31:42.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the real world in a proper fashion and when I say in a proper fashion I mean like human-like grasping of\N在现实世界中以恰当的方式，所谓恰当的方式，指的是类似人类般的抓取方式
Dialogue: 0,0:31:42.67,0:31:49.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,objects like how can we do this and this all started with me like playing around with Chet GPT and asking it hey\N像这样我们该怎么实现呢？这一切都始于我玩弄着Chet GPT，然后问它：嘿
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.97,0:31:56.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm a robot my owner told me to pick up a doll that lies in front of me where should I grasp it?\N我是个机器人，主人让我捡起面前的一个洋娃娃，我该从哪里抓它？
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.67,0:32:04.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then Chachupati in his usual way came back with, yes, like either use the arms, the bellacks, or the torso.\N然后查丘帕蒂一如既往地回来，说：“是的，要么用胳膊，要么用腰，要么用躯干。”
Dialogue: 0,0:32:04.23,0:32:06.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically don't grasp it at the head.\N基本上别从头上抓。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.31,0:32:10.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we started to think about this a little bit more and like built the system\N然后我们开始更深入地思考这个问题，并着手构建了这个系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.67,0:32:17.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,that you basically like provided with a prompt about the object to be grasped and then it came\N基本上你只需提供一个关于要抓取物体的提示，然后它就会执行
Dialogue: 0,0:32:17.67,0:32:23.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,back to us with like parts that we actually should maybe should grasp the object and then\N回到我们这边，拿那些我们实际上应该抓住物体的部件。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:23.90,0:32:30.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,now at that time we generated this 3D model SLAM by hand nowadays you would use a lot\N那时我们是手动构建这个3D模型的SLAM，如今你会用大量自动化工具。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:30.71,0:32:37.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,of vision language model for this like Sam 3D or whatsoever in order to generate these 3D\N用于生成这些3D内容的视觉语言模型，比如Sam 3D或其他类似模型
Dialogue: 0,0:32:37.17,0:32:42.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,point clouds but what is then behind this as well is grasp it which is a tool that\N点云，但其背后更重要的则是抓取，这是一款工具
Dialogue: 0,0:32:42.47,0:32:49.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,basically samples stable grasp points on 3D surfaces right you basically if you have a two finger\N基本上是在三维表面上采样稳定的抓取点，如果你有两个手指
Dialogue: 0,0:32:49.45,0:32:56.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,gripper it samples pairs of grasp points which are sufficient to basically keep the object in the hand.\N夹爪会采样一对抓取点，足以基本将物体固定在手中。
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.49,0:33:02.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And once you have this you can just check as to whether these grasp points fall into these green regions provided you by\N一旦你有了这些信息，只需检查这些抓取点是否落在所提供的绿色区域之内即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:02.13,0:33:11.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,the segmentation tool and then you accept only those that lie in green regions and all of a sudden you get semantic grasps.\N然后你只接受位于绿色区域内的分割结果，突然之间，你就得到了语义抓取。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:11.74,0:33:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,And here's the system in action.\N这就是系统运行的实况。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.78,0:33:17.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,So on the left-hand side is the purely geometric part,\N左边是纯粹的几何部分，
Dialogue: 0,0:33:17.60,0:33:23.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,on the right-hand side is line grasp and You can see is that all of this in a zero-shot fashion, right?\N右侧是零样本抓取，可以看到所有操作都是以零样本方式完成的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.14,0:33:29.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,so there's no training involved as directly operates on these on these objects and Yeah,\N因此，它无需训练，可直接作用于这些对象，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.86,0:33:35.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,particularly like the cactus down there or the cake is also pretty impressive And then on\N特别喜欢下面的仙人掌，或者蛋糕也相当令人印象深刻。然后在
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.76,0:33:42.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,the next slide you will also see the doll the candle is also like pretty interesting because\N下一页幻灯片中，你们还会看到这个玩偶，蜡烛也很有意思。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:42.34,0:33:47.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of the the system seems to seems to know that like a candle on a\N系统似乎知道，就像蜡烛放在上面一样
Dialogue: 0,0:33:47.29,0:33:52.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,candlestick is not very stable right so it basically will most likely fall off right so I\N蜡烛台不太稳，所以它很可能会掉下来。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:52.71,0:33:56.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,think this is where the power of these systems actually is when it comes to like\N这才是这些系统真正强大之处，尤其是在这方面。
Dialogue: 0,0:33:56.93,0:34:05.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,interacting with the real world this this capability of to actually perform like semantic or infer semantics\N与真实世界互动，这种能够实际执行并推断语义的能力
Dialogue: 0,0:34:05.43,0:34:12.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the individual objects sometimes whenever I see this or whenever I see these videos I start\N有时当我看到这些物体，或者看到这些视频时，我就会开始
Dialogue: 0,0:34:12.15,0:34:18.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,thinking oh my goodness that's this thing understands the world which is just crazy from my perspective.\N天啊，这东西竟然理解世界，从我的角度看简直太疯狂了。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:19.11,0:34:26.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just a side note here we also did a user study we asked users where to actually grasp individual objects like\N顺便提一下，我们还做了一项用户研究，询问用户实际抓取单个物体时应该从哪里下手。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:26.66,0:34:34.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,a value closer to one means that we are mostly corresponding with the places where the user would grasp the individual objects.\N越接近1的值意味着我们主要对应的是用户能够抓取单个物体的位置。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:34.22,0:34:41.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to pay a special attention to the toilet brush over here right and 97.6 %\N我想特别关注一下这里的马桶刷，它的使用率高达97.6%。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.86,0:34:48.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the User said they would grasp it at the handle and the other two points for it.\N用户说他们会握住把手，另外两个点用来固定。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.24,0:34:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically would also grasp it at the brush The reason for this might be that the picture that\N基本上也会在刷子处抓住它，原因可能是图片
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.76,0:34:59.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,we provided in the image showed a new toilet brush So that might be the excuse for this.\N图片中展示了一款新型马桶刷，这或许就是理由。
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.18,0:35:04.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But yes Just a small sight but you can go even more complex, right?\N但没错，虽然只是很小的一步，但你还能走得更复杂，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.92,0:35:10.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you have objects that are like substantially more complex when it comes to the reasoning\N如果你处理的对象在推理方面复杂得多
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.34,0:35:19.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,part you get relatively good annotation or answers about where to actually grasp these individual objects.\N你获得相对较好的标注或答案，了解如何实际抓取这些独立物体。
Dialogue: 0,0:35:19.26,0:35:23.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,This also works for placing like if you want to know how to place an object\N这同样适用于物体摆放，比如你想知道如何放置一个物体
Dialogue: 0,0:35:23.10,0:35:27.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,onto it onto a table then you can just ask these systems like how should I rotate\N把它放到桌子上，然后你就可以问这些系统：我该怎么旋转？
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.64,0:35:32.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,my arm in order to properly place this object onto the table and I think you\N我的手臂，以正确地将这个物体放到桌子上，我觉得你
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.60,0:35:37.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,need to click once in order to this happening and so based on this robot can actually\N需要点击一次才能触发，因此机器人可以据此实际执行
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.04,0:35:45.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,in a zero shot fashion execute these tasks which is pretty impressive in which I particularly\N以零样本方式执行这些任务，这非常令人印象深刻，尤其是这一点
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.08,0:35:53.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,like about these these foundation models right the next step is also something like kind of like\N就像这些基础模型一样，下一步也类似这样
Dialogue: 0,0:35:53.28,0:35:58.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,a message that I want to deliver so when you think about embodied AI and think about\N我想传达的一条信息是，当你思考具身AI时，请记住
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.72,0:36:06.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,that this basically means that we use our body to interact with the real world Then this,\N这意味着我们通过身体与现实世界进行交互。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:07.02,0:36:15.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,from my perspective, means more than just using positions and video and images.\N从我的角度来看，这远不止是使用位置、视频和图像那么简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:16.25,0:36:21.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,So when you see someone manipulating an object in YouTube,\N所以当你看到有人在 YouTube 上操作某个物体时，
Dialogue: 0,0:36:21.71,0:36:32.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,you actually do not know how much force this person applies and what it actually feels in order to manipulate this object in this particular form.\N你实际上并不知道这个人施加了多大的力，以及在这种特定形态下操作这个物体时的真实感受。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:32.63,0:36:34.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is something that is substantially missing.\N所以这正是目前严重缺失的部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:34.77,0:36:39.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know that some computer vision people argue that you actually don't need this.\N我知道有些计算机视觉领域的研究者认为，其实你根本不需要这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.99,0:36:41.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can do everything with vision.\N你可以用视觉完成一切。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:42.23,0:36:50.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,However, when you look at us, we don't run around all the time looking at our hands about what is going on in our hands.\N然而，当你观察我们时，我们并不会一直低头看手，去关注手上的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.01,0:36:53.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,We simply don't have the time for doing this.\N我们根本没有时间来做这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:53.37,0:36:59.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And it would be computationally simply too expensive and we would maybe also run into things and hurt ourselves.\N而且计算上会过于昂贵，我们还可能撞到东西，伤到自己。
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.15,0:37:10.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So on top of this, you could argue, or you can argue, that there are many people in the world who don't have vision and still live a decent life.\N此外，你可以说，世界上有很多人虽然没有视力，却依然能过上体面的生活。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:10.97,0:37:15.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's very, very few people in the world who don't have tactile information.\N但世界上几乎没有人缺乏触觉信息。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.01,0:37:23.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe, like, tactile information is more important than actually, like, we currently believe.\N所以，也许触觉信息的重要性，比我们目前认为的还要大。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:23.83,0:37:27.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is why we started this project, Flow Touch,\N这就是我们启动这个项目“流触”的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.25,0:37:34.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we are trying to predict what the world will feel like when we touch it with our sensors at a certain place.\N我们正试图预测，当我们在某个位置用传感器触碰世界时，世界会是什么感觉。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:35.31,0:37:39.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alright, so what we want to do is we want to basically predict the sense of touch,\N好吧，我们想做的就是基本预测触觉感知。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:39.63,0:37:45.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,like when, from an actual perspective, anywhere on the object and even for novel objects.\N比如从物体的实际视角来看，无论是在物体的哪个位置，甚至对于新物体也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:45.73,0:37:50.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is something that, from my perspective, is super important.\N从我的角度来看，这一点非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:50.43,0:37:52.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Predictions are always important.\N预测始终非常重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:52.13,0:37:55.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you are able to predict something, you have the basis for planning.\N当你能够预测某件事时，你就有了规划的基础。
Dialogue: 0,0:37:56.71,0:38:00.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,When you know what it's going to feel like and what your tactile perceptions are,\N当你知道它会带来怎样的感受以及你的触觉感知时，
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.25,0:38:06.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,when you grasp something, you actually get an idea as to whether this grasp is going to be stable or not.\N当你抓住某物时，实际上就能判断这个抓握是否稳定。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:07.09,0:38:10.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is the reason why we actually looked into this.\N所以这就是我们实际上研究这个问题的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:10.67,0:38:19.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we started with looking at the so-called vision-based tactile sensors and like all visual tactile sensors that\N我们一开始研究的是所谓的视觉触觉传感器，就像所有视觉触觉传感器一样
Dialogue: 0,0:38:19.66,0:38:25.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,provide you basically with an image and which is why this is so super hyped right now in the computer\N基本上给你一张图像，这就是为什么现在计算机领域对此如此热捧的原因。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.96,0:38:34.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,vision a community because like that what they are super straight when is basically processing images so this is what\N视觉化一个社区，因为它们本质上就是处理图像的，所以这就是……
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.52,0:38:42.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,we are doing in this in this work here tactile sensor prediction we are basically combining not only real world data\N我们在此项工作中，通过触觉传感器预测，基本上结合了真实世界的数据
Dialogue: 0,0:38:43.00,0:38:53.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,plus the grasping points and the simulation data in order to actually train this this predictor turns out that the\N再加上抓取点和仿真数据，才能真正训练出这个预测模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.29,0:38:58.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,results are pretty good there's one thing that we would like to understand a little bit better so we have\N结果相当不错，不过我们还想更深入地理解一件事，那就是我们
Dialogue: 0,0:38:58.47,0:39:09.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,this technique called domain conditioning which actually provides us with the best vision based metrics on these predictions but it's\N这种技术称为领域调节，实际上为我们提供了这些预测中最优的基于视觉的指标
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.50,0:39:18.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually not better than that what we call tactile loss that we added in order to further improve the tactile perceptions.\N实际上，这并不比我们为进一步提升触觉感知而引入的触觉损失更好。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:19.37,0:39:23.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there is something that we still need to work on we are not quite there but\N所以我们还有些事情需要继续努力，目前还没到理想状态。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:23.95,0:39:29.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,this is like even this entire space is relatively at the beginning of what is being done.\N这个领域整体上还处于起步阶段。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:30.84,0:39:38.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,The next part that I mentioned as well is forces right and I think this Truly believe this is\N我提到的下一部分是力量，我认为这确实至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:39:38.26,0:39:43.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,a limitation of that what we are right doing right now we are mostly or too much focusing on like\N我们目前所做事情的一个局限是，我们大多或过于专注于
Dialogue: 0,0:39:43.86,0:39:53.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,vision and in positions only and we urgently need to go dive deeper into robotics and look into like\N视觉和位置信息，我们迫切需要深入探索机器人技术，深入研究类似
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.58,0:40:03.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,More multimodal or higher multimodality basically incorporating tactile information and forces as well Just to give you one idea about,\N更多模态或更高程度的多模态，基本上还包括触觉信息和受力情况，仅举一个例子供你参考，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:03.66,0:40:08.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,like, what the effect of this might be, here's this relatively recent work, like RANCH Act,\N比如，这种影响可能是什么样的，这里有一项相对较新的研究，比如RANCH法案，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.28,0:40:15.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,where we enhance robot policies for contact-rich behavior using actually direct RANCH control.\N我们通过实际的直接RANCH控制，增强机器人在高接触场景下的策略。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.86,0:40:21.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,What is nowadays being done mostly is that contact forces are dealt\N如今大多是在处理接触力方面。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:21.22,0:40:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,with implicitly by using position control plus controlling the stiffness of the robot,\N通过使用位置控制并调节机器人的刚度来隐式实现，
Dialogue: 0,0:40:26.24,0:40:26.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,which, however,\N然而，这
Dialogue: 0,0:40:27.00,0:40:31.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,can be problematic when it comes to different applications where you actually need different\N在涉及不同应用时可能存在问题，因为实际上你需要不同的解决方案。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.88,0:40:41.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,forces for the manipulation tasks and so long speech short message but what we are\N用于操作任务的力，以及长时间的语音，简短的信息，但我们正在
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.26,0:40:48.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,doing replacing here is basically position with only with with with expertise oh yeah adding\N这里替换基本上是仅凭经验来操作，没错，就是加进去。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.58,0:40:54.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,basically forces to that, and we are doing this on top of this policy ACT\N本质上是强制执行这一政策，而我们正在此基础上推进。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.86,0:41:01.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,and basically like going from position to force torque there's this one problem there that\N基本上从位置到力矩的转换存在一个问题
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.95,0:41:05.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,we properly need to deal with free space when the robot is not like touching\N当机器人并未接触时，我们必须正确处理自由空间问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:05.55,0:41:12.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,anything or then you basically need to introduce a heuristic and dampening the entire system\N否则你基本上就得引入一个启发式方法，并对整个系统进行阻尼处理
Dialogue: 0,0:41:13.01,0:41:19.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then that allows us then to execute this entire task then in force mode.\N然后我们就能以力控模式执行整个任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.63,0:41:26.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Alright so the we are playing here it's like we're training this with a like leader follower setting and then he has\N好的，我们这里玩的是类似领导-跟随的训练模式，然后他有
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.31,0:41:36.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,a few experimental results regarding this basically showing that in most cases we obtain a substantial increase in performance which clearly shows\N一些实验结果基本表明，在大多数情况下，我们都能显著提升性能，这显然得到了证实。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:36.05,0:41:45.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,that going over to force control is actually like super beneficial and super helpful and this also our chance to set ourselves\N转向力控实际上非常有益，也极为有帮助，这同样也是我们确立自身定位的绝佳机会。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:45.13,0:41:53.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,apart from that what has gone in the computer vision space where we are mostly about position and and computer vision only.\N除此之外，计算机视觉领域还发生了什么？我们主要关注的是位置和计算机视觉本身。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:55.10,0:42:01.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah here's a few tasks that we could do with these with these robots they are like aligned to the Collaboration with\N是的，我们可以让这些机器人完成一些任务，它们与协作非常契合。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.12,0:42:12.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,Siemens and they are pretty much interested in more industrial applications of of this So which brings us also to this form\N西门子也对这类技术在工业领域的更多应用很感兴趣，这也让我们关注到这种形态。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:12.33,0:42:20.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,of like refining policies and and and then also like Trying\N比如优化策略，还有尝试
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.33,0:42:25.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,to adjust robots based on given Vision language action models for\N根据给定的视觉-语言-动作模型调整机器人
Dialogue: 0,0:42:25.41,0:42:33.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,example in order to perform or get better in their tasks It's something that I would like to not only see in manipulation,\N例如，为了更好地完成或提升任务表现，这正是我希望不仅在操作中看到的。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:33.17,0:42:42.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,but also in navigation Particularly when there are no maps in the game So this is some work where we basically which is called refined\N而是在导航方面，尤其是在游戏中没有地图的情况下。这是一些我们称之为精细化的工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:42.27,0:42:50.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,policy distillation where we are actually trying to like become faster when it\N策略蒸馏，我们实际上是在尝试变得更快
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.06,0:42:54.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,comes to the adjustment or fine-tuning of these models to specific tasks,\N在将这些模型调整或微调以适应特定任务时，
Dialogue: 0,0:42:54.40,0:43:00.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,right which normally fine-tuning actually takes a lot of data and also\N这通常需要大量数据，而微调恰恰也是如此。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:00.36,0:43:07.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,doing this from scratch with reinforcement learning typically requires also a lot of exploration.\N通过强化学习从零开始实现，通常还需要大量的探索。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:07.44,0:43:13.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we're doing here basically is we are combining this on policy reinforcement learning with behavioral cloning,\N我们在这里所做的，本质上是将策略上的强化学习与行为克隆相结合。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:13.98,0:43:21.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,introducing an additional loss down here and by doing so we are basically getting substantially more\N在这里增加一个额外的损失项，这样我们基本上能获得显著更多的效果
Dialogue: 0,0:43:21.12,0:43:30.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,effective in certain learning tasks or fine-tuning tasks compared to existing baselines like for example PPO,\N在某些学习任务或微调任务中，相较于现有的基线方法（例如 PPO），表现更有效。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:30.64,0:43:32.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,which our system is relying upon.\N我们的系统所依赖的。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:34.01,0:43:41.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is an interesting application towards like getting more efficient and this is also something that we actually should do.\N这是一个很有意义的应用，有助于提高效率，同时也确实是我们应该去做的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.32,0:43:48.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,The other question is like, how can we actually do this, what is the best way of doing this,\N另一个问题是，我们到底该如何实现这一点，什么方法才是最佳方案？
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.09,0:43:54.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,this reinforcement learning in order to fine-tune, in, for example, existing policies.\N通过强化学习来微调现有策略，例如。
Dialogue: 0,0:43:54.23,0:44:03.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in this context, we would like to mention a relatively recent task, recent work that we are carrying out right now,\N在这种背景下，我想提一下一项相对较新的任务，也就是我们目前正在开展的一项研究工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:03.61,0:44:09.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,like in this question of developing policies that generalize better to environmental\N就像在制定那些能更好地泛化到环境中的政策时一样
Dialogue: 0,0:44:09.13,0:44:14.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,changes or to tasks that are actually not really seen by the robot.\N或对机器人实际上并未观察到的任务进行更改。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:14.75,0:44:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how can we do this more quickly with a few user demonstrations only?\N我们该如何仅通过少量用户演示就更快地实现这一点？
Dialogue: 0,0:44:19.47,0:44:24.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the idea there is that to basically predict the reward signal, right,\N核心思想是，基本上预测奖励信号，对吧，
Dialogue: 0,0:44:24.59,0:44:31.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,in order to actually better understand what the individual task is with the underline\N为了真正更好地理解每个任务的具体内容，需要弄清楚下划线部分的含义
Dialogue: 0,0:44:31.19,0:44:36.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,hypothesis there is that learning the reward is simpler than actually learning the entire control.\N有一种假设认为，学习奖励比学习完整的控制要简单。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.89,0:44:44.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's so and what we are using for this purpose is basically human demonstrations and the basic idea\N而且我们为此所使用的方法基本上是人类示范，其基本理念是
Dialogue: 0,0:44:44.31,0:44:52.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,is as with a longer task demonstrated by a human right the further you go along this this task execution\N就像人类完成一项较长任务时所展示的那样，任务执行得越深入，表现就越明显。
Dialogue: 0,0:44:52.11,0:44:59.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,the higher the performance of the the agent actually is in the case where this is successful which we\N代理的实际性能越高，这种情况成功时的表现就越出色
Dialogue: 0,0:44:59.19,0:45:04.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,would assume in most of the demonstrations so it's what this allows you to is basically to get kind of\N在大多数演示中都会默认，这实际上让你基本上能够获得一种类似的效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:04.87,0:45:11.68,Sub,,0,0,0,,like binary values or a pair of values where the later one is typically higher than the former one\N类似于二进制值，或一对数值，其中后者通常高于前者
Dialogue: 0,0:45:11.73,0:45:18.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,and if you learn a reward function from this you can actually execute a task and at the same time\N如果你从这些数据中学习到一个奖励函数，实际上就可以执行任务，同时
Dialogue: 0,0:45:18.71,0:45:27.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,estimate the reward signal that the agent would get through this image substantially helps performing reinforcement learning and the\N通过这张图像估算智能体可能获得的奖励信号，能显著提升强化学习的效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:27.05,0:45:37.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,nice aspect of this is that the current S implementation runs super efficiently on actually a low performance laptop computer.\N这一点很出色，当前的 S 实现能在实际的低性能笔记本电脑上运行得非常高效。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.54,0:45:46.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's talk about the recent news and I think this is a super important problem that we are right now facing.\N我们来谈谈最近的新闻，我认为这是我们目前正面临的一个极其重要的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.72,0:45:56.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,So to be honest I was a little bit shocked over the past few weeks and whenever you read the news then I let it get a little bit\N说实话，过去几周我有点震惊，每当看到新闻时，我都会忍不住多想一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.26,0:46:05.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,scared about like where this is all going right so we right now see a little bit of a headwind right and that and we are also facing the risk\N担心这一切会走向何方，所以目前我们看到一点逆风，而且我们也面临着风险
Dialogue: 0,0:46:05.94,0:46:16.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,that maybe our societies will not really be happy with that what is help going on in this space of of AI it's all using a lot of energy\N也许我们的社会并不会真正对这种情况感到满意，因为AI领域正在消耗大量能源。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.70,0:46:22.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,and then there's also some companies who let their interns go wild with their with\N还有些公司会让实习生自由发挥，尽情尝试。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:22.42,0:46:27.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,their with their agents and producing all kind of things that we don't really like.\N它们通过自己的智能体制造出各种我们并不喜欢的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.10,0:46:38.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so this is something that we maybe as like researchers also put should put more attention not only being more reasonable with\N因此，作为研究人员，我们也应该更加关注这一点，而不仅仅是在合理性上有所提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.34,0:46:45.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,our tools but also looking into what is actually going on there and how can we understand these agents in a better fashion.\N我们的工具，还深入探究那里实际发生的情况，以及如何更好地理解这些智能体。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:46.42,0:46:50.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this is some work that there's some work that we recently did in this space basically\N这是一些我们最近在这个领域完成的工作，基本上是这样
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.70,0:46:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,trying to understand what these agents actually learned and what they're actually focusing on in their work.\N试图弄清楚这些智能体究竟学到了什么，以及它们在工作中真正关注的是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.16,0:47:08.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is a work that we're basically trying to, for these vision language navigation models, to figure out what they're actually focusing on.\N所以我们正在做的这项工作，本质上是想弄清楚这些视觉语言导航模型实际关注的是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.16,0:47:12.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what are the parameters that are important for these models?\N那么，这些模型中重要的参数有哪些？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:13.16,0:47:19.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so for those who don't know vision language navigation systems, they're basically taking multimodal input,\N因此，对于不了解视觉语言导航系统的人来说，它们本质上是接收多模态输入。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.46,0:47:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,in many cases the current observation plus history, and then a language instruction,\N在许多情况下，当前观测值加上历史信息，再结合语言指令，
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.28,0:47:30.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,which can be turned right at the door, very simple or go through the corridor,\N可以在门口直接右转，非常简单，或者穿过走廊。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.61,0:47:35.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,enter the kitchen, go past the table in the kitchen and stop in front of the fridge.\N进入厨房，绕过厨房里的桌子，停在冰箱前面。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.91,0:47:38.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,It could be a little bit more complicated actually.\N实际上可能稍微复杂一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:39.13,0:47:45.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the question then is, what actually drives these navigation decisions?\N那么问题来了，究竟是什么真正驱动了这些导航决策？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.21,0:47:47.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,What do these systems rely on?\N这些系统依赖于什么？
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.05,0:47:52.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And there we used partially standard techniques to analyze this in our study.\N在我们的研究中，我们采用了部分标准化技术来分析这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:52.59,0:48:00.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we basically looked at, for example, the visual focus and try to understand what do these systems actually look at.\N所以我们基本上分析了视觉焦点，试图弄清楚这些系统实际上在关注什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.17,0:48:06.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,So given this observation here what you can basically do is like blur individual areas of these\N基于这一观察，你基本上可以对这些区域进行局部模糊处理
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.43,0:48:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,images and then try to figure out under which in which cases the agent actually changes its decisions.\N然后尝试弄清楚在哪些情况下，智能体实际上改变了它的决策。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:14.79,0:48:20.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which basically would mean that this corresponding area and the image would be relevant for generating that decision.\N这基本上意味着，该对应区域和图像将与生成该决策相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:20.99,0:48:23.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's one thing that you could do.\N这是一件你可以做到的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.51,0:48:28.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can do this is the same with the textual focus you can just remove individual words from the\N你也可以用同样的方法对文本焦点进行操作，只需删除个别词语即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.97,0:48:37.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,text description or tokens and then get an idea about which token slash words are relevant for the navigation task.\N文本描述或词元，然后了解哪些词元或词语与导航任务相关。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.85,0:48:45.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we did on top of this is what we added a human mask where we basically like annotated in the image what we think\N我们在此基础上所做的，是添加了一个人脸掩码，基本上就是在图像中标注出我们认为的关键区域。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.87,0:48:55.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,are the areas that are relevant for the navigation task but that we would maybe focus our attention on when we perform this navigation task.\N这些是与导航任务相关，但在执行导航任务时我们可能会集中注意力的区域。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.95,0:48:58.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the output of this was pretty interesting.\N而这一结果相当有趣。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.11,0:49:08.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So turns out that the precision on visual and textual heat maps is less than 70 % on these state-of-the-art models,\N结果发现，这些最前沿模型在视觉和文本热图上的精度低于70%。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.37,0:49:13.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,which basically these models, to a large extent, focus on things that we find irrelevant.\N这些模型在很大程度上关注的，恰恰是我们认为无关紧要的事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.59,0:49:20.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's kind of like something that we would actually need to understand a little bit better.\N所以这有点像是我们需要更好地理解的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:20.69,0:49:28.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you can do this for images and text as well And then you can also look at the history and basically ask\N你也可以对图像和文本进行同样的操作，然后查看历史记录，基本上可以提问
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.47,0:49:36.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,yourself What which parts of the history or how much does the history actually influence the decisions of these of these agents and?\N你自己，历史的哪些部分，或者历史在多大程度上实际上影响了这些智能体的决策？
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.33,0:49:44.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,like it's an increasing amount like blur the all the past images to figure out under which like Like how\N就像逐渐增多一样，模糊所有过去的图像，以弄清楚在什么情况下……
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.15,0:49:49.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,many images you need to blur to actually of the history to actually make Confuse the agent and make it take\N你需要模糊大量图像，才能真正混淆智能体，让它出错。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:49.37,0:49:57.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,false decisions Right and it turns out that all agents are actually sensitive to a visual memory correct corruption Which is\N错误的决策，而且事实证明，所有智能体实际上都对视觉记忆的错误篡改敏感。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.81,0:50:07.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,good because we now see that they actually need history to actually make their decisions Although this is on different scales,\N很好，因为我们现在发现，他们实际上需要历史数据才能做出决策。尽管这涉及不同的尺度。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:07.64,0:50:12.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,but what we also found is that while they are sensitive to history changes\N但我们还发现，它们对历史变化也十分敏感
Dialogue: 0,0:50:13.32,0:50:19.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are situations in there basically pretty robust to blurring all images so the\N其中有一些情况，基本上对图像模糊具有很强的鲁棒性。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:19.16,0:50:29.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,decline like it's not very much so I would at least have expected a little bit more which is also kind of like impressive so from my perspective\N下降得并不明显，所以我至少期望能多一些，这其实也挺令人印象深刻的，至少从我的角度来看是这样。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.18,0:50:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,that clearly shows that we need to understand more like we need to understand\N这清楚地表明，我们需要更深入地理解，就像我们需要更深入地理解一样
Dialogue: 0,0:50:33.36,0:50:37.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,better what is actually going on in these models in order to actually also\N更好地理解这些模型内部实际发生的情况，从而真正实现突破
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.80,0:50:42.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,better explain them to our society to better explain what is what is actually\N更好地向我们的社会解释它们，以更清楚地说明实际情况是什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:42.28,0:50:46.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,going on there and maybe also to explain what these models are basically doing.\N继续进行，也许还能解释一下这些模型本质上在做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:47.46,0:50:56.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's also another aspect that we looked into this context which is called activation steering where with this specific\N我们还研究了这一情境下的另一个方面，称为激活控制，通过这种特定方法可以实现对模型激活的调节。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.60,0:51:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,aware VLN and so the idea there is or some of these models can perform that what is called reasoning.\N意识到视觉语言导航，因此这些模型中的一些能够执行所谓的推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:05.14,0:51:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,They basically instead of like generating these navigation actions they then generate a sentence like I'm confused\N他们基本上不是生成这些导航动作，而是生成一句“我有点困惑”的话。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:13.78,0:51:19.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,which then in a multi-agent setting might lead to actually additional reasoning and like basically going\N在多智能体环境下，这可能会带来额外的推理，本质上相当于进一步深入思考。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:19.88,0:51:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,back to this type of free planning and this question that the problem that we figured out\N回到这种自由规划，以及我们所发现的这个问题
Dialogue: 0,0:51:25.20,0:51:32.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,is when These training and deployment distributions were too different than the agent actually never generated reasoning,\N当训练和部署的分布差异过大时，智能体实际上从未生成过推理过程。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.06,0:51:42.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is kind of like crazy and so the what we experimented with is like can we actually like enforce this\N这听起来有点疯狂，所以我们尝试了一下，看看能不能真的强制执行这一点。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.26,0:51:51.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,type of like reasoning and this actually like that was we found out like with these latent vector steering that we could\N一种类似推理的方式，实际上我们发现，通过这些潜在向量的引导，我们可以做到这一点
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.20,0:52:00.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually correct this and make this agent generate like reasoning in order to basically replant its actions which is also kind\N实际上，纠正这一点，让这个智能体在生成时进行推理，从而从根本上重新规划其行为。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.94,0:52:11.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,of like an interesting technique for like revising false decisions of these agents okay in general like we found that modality helps,\N一种有趣的技巧，用于修正这些智能体的错误决策。总的来说，我们发现模态有助于提升效果。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.76,0:52:21.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of them are steerable and then they not always behave like humans, what concerns at least me a little bit.\N其中一些是可以操控的，但它们的行为并不总是像人类一样，这至少让我有点担心。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.14,0:52:27.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Finally I want to talk a little bit about infrastructures in the last three or four minutes.\N最后，我想在接下来三到四分钟里简单谈一下基础设施。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:27.46,0:52:35.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's we are also working on building infrastructure for like improving robot development in the future.\N因此，我们也在致力于构建基础设施，以促进未来机器人开发的提升。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:35.82,0:52:43.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,One system is the so-called robot control stack for learning over robot learning at scale\N一个系统是所谓的机器人控制栈，用于在大规模机器人学习中实现学习。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.50,0:52:51.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,it is actually designed to support like different sensors actuators robots switching between sim and real tail\N它实际上被设计用于支持不同传感器、执行器和机器人在仿真与现实之间的切换。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.60,0:52:59.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,operation and data collection and also policy deployment and it runs on different types of hardware we\N运行和数据收集，以及策略部署，可在不同类型的硬件上运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:59.42,0:53:06.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,also provide the corresponding simulations to this and it's also like it's been used in different applications,\N同时提供相应的仿真，并且它也被应用于不同场景。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:06.98,0:53:16.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,teleoperated and scripted data collection, training, reinforcement learning, and VLA inferences in different settings.\N在不同场景下的遥操作与脚本化数据采集、训练、强化学习以及视觉-语言-动作模型推理。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.85,0:53:24.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And recently, it has also been applied to Dieter Foxen's Toy Blocks World, which was published last year.\N最近，它还被应用于去年发表的迪特·福肯的积木世界。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.05,0:53:29.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I'm mentioning this here as a homage to my dear friend Dieter.\N我在这里提到这一点，是向我亲爱的朋友迪特尔致敬。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.69,0:53:32.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And by the way, tomorrow will be his 60th birthday.\N顺便说一下，明天就是他60岁的生日了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.71,0:53:42.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,So don't miss to congratulate him tomorrow and thank you Dieter and all the best for tomorrow I hope you will get many best wishes and yeah,\N所以别忘了明天向他表示祝贺，谢谢迪特尔，祝你明天一切顺利，希望你能收到许多美好的祝福，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.41,0:53:47.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,thank you for all your hard work also in robotics and Then the other one is this dual\N感谢大家在机器人领域的辛勤付出，还有这个双模态的
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.33,0:53:55.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,bench benchmark that we recently developed the benchmark that goes beyond just single arm benchmarks we have we actually\N我们最近开发的基准测试，超越了单一机械臂测试，实际上我们已经实现了
Dialogue: 0,0:53:55.89,0:54:03.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,also looked into a different like success rate for a failure analysis where we actually not only looked\N还研究了另一种失败分析的成功率，我们不仅进行了分析
Dialogue: 0,0:54:03.53,0:54:11.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,at the final The final task completion but also intermediate stages that the robots were supposed to execute Yes,\N最终任务的完成，还包括机器人应执行的中间阶段。是的，
Dialogue: 0,0:54:11.49,0:54:12.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the setup.\N设置好了。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:12.55,0:54:18.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is running in simulation But also in in the real world and these assets\N所以这在仿真中运行，也在现实世界中运行，这些资产
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.09,0:54:23.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,that you see there are all 3d printable so you can actually Download the specifications and\N你看到的都是可3D打印的，你可以实际下载其规格。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:23.37,0:54:29.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,generate these setups on the the robots that you do have at home And we're supporting\N在你家现有的机器人上生成这些设置，我们正在提供支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.87,0:54:36.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,different types of tasks over here which are all listed on this on this Slide here.\N这里列出了各种不同类型的任务，都在这张幻灯片上。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:36.64,0:54:44.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,All right, and some results are also provided turns out that Like low data fine-tuning is problematic.\N好的，一些结果也已提供，结果表明，低数据微调存在问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:44.54,0:54:49.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's what we find and grasping and early stages are bottlenecked Potentially because\N这就是我们发现的情况，而早期阶段的掌握和理解可能因某些原因受阻。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:49.64,0:54:52.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,in later stages all the robot has to do is to drop objects which\N在后期阶段，机器人只需将物体放下即可。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.64,0:54:57.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,is much easier than grasping them and manipulating things but there's something that we\N比抓取和操作物体要容易得多，但其中有些东西是我们
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.52,0:55:04.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,would like to look into even further good let's skip this here another task\N我想进一步探讨一下，好吧，我们跳过这个，来看另一个任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:04.50,0:55:07.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,that I've been doing other thing that I've been doing over the past years\N这些年我一直在做其他事情
Dialogue: 0,0:55:07.30,0:55:14.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,is actually improving computing infrastructure in Bavaria this is a project that I've done\N实际上，我正在改善巴伐利亚的计算基础设施，这是一个我参与的项目。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.28,0:55:19.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,together with Björn Ommer, this is a so-called Bavarian foundation model project that\N与比约恩·奥默共同推进的，是一个所谓的巴伐利亚基础模型项目
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.86,0:55:28.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,machine that you see here is 400 B100 GPUs that was bought by the\N你看到的这台机器，是英伟达购买的400块B100 GPU。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:28.76,0:55:33.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,state of Bavaria and right now we are getting an additional number of thousand\N巴伐利亚州目前正额外增加数千名人员
Dialogue: 0,0:55:33.74,0:55:39.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,GB 200 GPUs delivered which is Peter Stone mentioned this earlier this morning like\N已交付的 GB 200 GPU，正如彼得·斯通今早早些时候提到的那样
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.22,0:55:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,about the infrastructure that they have and we are going to have probably one\N关于他们所拥有的基础设施，以及我们可能将要拥有的
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.24,0:55:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the largest compute infrastructures on the university scale in in Germany and Which\N德国规模最大的大学级计算基础设施之一
Dialogue: 0,0:55:51.12,0:55:58.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,brings me to the end of this talk I truly believe that we need to actually join forces as a society in At this discussion last night about\N让我讲到结尾，我真心认为，我们作为社会成员，必须真正携手，共同参与昨晚关于这一议题的讨论。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:58.54,0:56:06.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,how we can actually keep up with everything that is going on in in the industry And where is robot learning going to be in like for academic?\N我们该如何真正跟上行业内的所有进展？在学术领域，机器人学习又将走向何方？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:07.00,0:56:10.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Robot learning research going to be and there are so many companies in this\N机器人学习研究将大有可为，而且这一领域已有众多公司涉足。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.76,0:56:15.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,space that have large teams and can carry out large-scale projects instead of and\N拥有大型团队并能开展大规模项目的地方，而不是其他地方。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:15.82,0:56:20.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,while we are having to deal with actually these type of PhD type projects\N而我们却不得不应对这类博士级别的项目
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.24,0:56:27.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,that are way more challenging and not on this big scale as the big Developments,\N这些挑战要大得多，而且不像那些大型开发项目那样规模庞大。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.42,0:56:28.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,right and in a few words,\N对，简单来说就是
Dialogue: 0,0:56:29.02,0:56:36.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think we again need to create a robotics foundation model including forces and sense\N我认为我们再次需要创建一个包含力和感知的机器人基础模型
Dialogue: 0,0:56:36.44,0:56:41.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,of touch I used to say we need a son of robotics and and like\N触觉方面，我过去常说，我们需要一个机器人之子，就像这样
Dialogue: 0,0:56:41.69,0:56:46.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,building something like this again these open max embodiment project which I really really liked\N再次打造这样的东西，比如这个我非常喜欢的开源最大具身项目
Dialogue: 0,0:56:46.57,0:56:50.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,and I think the only way to actually keep up with that what is going\N我认为唯一能真正跟上这种发展的方法是
Dialogue: 0,0:56:50.37,0:56:56.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,on industry is doing further projects like this and maybe also publishing this in the\N在产业界，正开展更多类似项目，或许还会将其发表出来。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:56.47,0:57:02.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,transactions on robotic and not only in a small conference and if all of this\N机器人领域的交易，而不仅仅是在一个小规模的会议上
Dialogue: 0,0:57:02.87,0:57:11.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,is going to be successful, then at least this is my hope: in the end we are going to be done with Probabilistic Robotics\N如果一切顺利，至少这是我所希望的：最终我们将告别概率机器人学。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.53,0:57:19.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,That is one of the favorite animations for students and I let this book basically explode here and that\N这是学生们最喜欢的一个动画，我让这本书在这里基本炸开了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.47,0:57:24.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,what we hopefully get out of this community is that this boulder is on top of the hill and\N我们希望从这个社区得到的是，这块巨石正位于山顶之上。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.99,0:57:33.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,with the robotics being solved and what I particularly like about this AI generated picture is this UTN symbol\N随着机器人技术的突破，我特别喜欢这张AI生成的图片，其中的UTN标志非常醒目。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.31,0:57:41.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,here which I didn't ask technology in Nuremberg research is so important that it needs to be on this robot.\N这里我想说的是，纽伦堡的研究技术如此重要，必须搭载在这台机器人上。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:41.65,0:57:42.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you for listening.\N谢谢聆听。
